# ── 2. Endurant ⊥ Perdurant (the continuant/occurrent divide) ────────────────────
# logic:Endurant's skos:definition contrasts logic:Perdurant, which has temporal
# parts. This candidate harvests that contrast into logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith
# logic:Perdurant, enforced by the native DL coherence gate.

logic:cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "endurant/perdurant disjointness holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Endurant and NOT logic:Perdurant (a continuant wholly present at each moment) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because a thing either endures through change or unfolds through it, not both."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "endurant/perdurant clash is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Endurant and logic:Perdurant is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant is asserted. A thing that is at once wholly present at every moment and composed of temporal parts is not an admissible model. The boundary the continuant/occurrent divide enforces."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateEndurantPerdurantDisjoint
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
