    skos:definition "The positive competency case the event/situation disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Event and NOT logic:Situation (a perdurant occurrence composed of temporal parts) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because an occurrence that unfolds in time is not the static configuration a situation records."@x-gmeow-english .

