# ── 4. Entity sortal covering (OWL-projection-only, NON-monotone) ────────────────
# Every gmeow:Entity is one of {Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject,
# SocialObject}. This covering is realized only in the OWL projection as an
# owl:unionOf and is DISCLOSED in the loss ledger; the native monotone chase does
# NOT enforce disjunctive covering. NO harvest back-link (the covering is not a
# single-field annotation). Category: necessary condition; risk: projection-only.

logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "entity sortal covering holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the entity-sortal covering must satisfy: a gmeow:Entity that is one of the four sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; it is the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "entity sortal covering gap is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the entity-sortal covering must respect: a gmeow:Entity typed into NONE of the four sortals violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering (a disjunction in the head is non-Horn), so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection, not in the native chase, and is disclosed in the loss ledger accordingly."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateEntitySortalCovering
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
