    skos:definition "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every gmeow:Entity is one of {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject}. Its source is gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse prose, which enumerates the four sortals. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf (a class-covering disjunction); it is NON-monotone and is disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link (the covering is a doc-level enumeration, not a single harvestable axiom field). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:howToUse text for drift detection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:349511ccdf3a10b7ce908e62ee66b4102b0469b4b54b191148d817380a8b96ae"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "read from gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse annotation, which enumerates the four sortals (Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject, SocialObject); the covering is realized in the OWL projection (owl:unionOf), is non-monotone, and is disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "covering: every gmeow:Entity is one of {Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject, SocialObject}"^^xsd:string ;
